STEP 1 — Create DynamoDB Table
-----------------------------
Table name : employees
Partition key: id [String]

STEP 2 — Create SQS Queue
-------------------------

Create Queue: employee-queue
Type: Standard
Keep all defaults

STEP 3 — Create Producer Lambda [It receives data from UI --> API gateway(in json) --> This Lambda will get data and add to SQS]
----------------------------
Create IAM ROLE
TE = Lambda
Permissions = SQSfullaccess, DynamoDBFullaccess
Name: employee-producer
Runtime: Python 3.14
Role: select role
Add Environment Variable in Lambda
---------------------
Configuration → Environment variables
QUEUE_URL = https://sqs.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/289857919920/employee-queue

Deploy function.
STEP4— Create Consumer Lambda [This lambda will collect data from SQS and store to DynamoDB]
Deploy.
STEP 5— Connect SQS Trigger
----------------------------
Open employee-consumer

Add Trigger --> Select SQS --> employee-queue --> Enable trigger.

In SQS , trigger added automatically [ SQS → Lambda automatically ]

STEP5 — Create Fetch Lambda
-----------------------------
Name : get-employees
Runtime: Python 3.14
ROLE: select role
DEPLOY
STEP 6 — Create API Gateway
---------------------------
We will create

POST /register
GET  /employees


Create --> HTTP API --> Build
API name: employee-api
Add integrations --> Lambda --> employee-producer --> Next

Add Route --> POST --> Resource path = /register , integration target = employee-producer --> next

Configure stages --> Remove $default stage --> Next --> Create


Left side --> Routes --> Create a route --> GET -> /employees --> Create
Left side ---> integrations --> Select /employees --> GET --> Create and attach integration
Attach this integration to a route = GET /employees
Integration type = Lambda
Select = get-employees

Left Side --> CORS --> Configure
Access-Control-Allow-Origin = *
Access-Control-Allow-Headers = *
Access-Control-Allow-Methods = GET POST


Left side ---> Deploy --> stage 
Create Stage --> Name: prod --> keep all defaults and create
DEPLOY --> select prod --> deploy

get the URL  : https://b70981n5vh.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod
